# A cannonball must reach a named chunk and damage the building there.
#
# Every assertion here failed at some point during development: the shot
# reached nothing, the aim pointed at open ground, or the ball was correct on
# the server and invisible. Naming the chunk is what makes "it hit" checkable.

report                    # the intact city

look 0.8 0                # face the facade
probe                     # say what is actually under the crosshair
aim 0 5810                # now aim at that chunk by identity
verify-aim 0 5810         # and refuse to continue if the ray misses it

fire ball
wait 120

# Contact, measured at the bonds rather than at the chunk. `expect-detached
# 0 5810` also passed while the ball was 0.6 m across and 7.1 t, and stopped
# passing at 0.3 m and 10.65 t: the narrower ball lands its larger impulse on
# fewer bonds, so it breaks 51 here where the wider one broke 71 and no longer
# takes that particular chunk off. Not tunnelling -- slowing the ball to 30 and
# 20 m/s reduced the damage to 2 bonds and then 0, which is momentum.
expect-bonds 20
report
